  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Vertical Cut Reveal\n\nLetters, words or whole lines slide up from behind an invisible cut line with a spring, staggered from the first, last, center or in random order; several lines follow one another.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A headline of one to a few lines should be revealed by pieces sliding up (or down) out of a hard-edged cut.\n- You need to choose how the pieces are split (letters, words, lines) and where the stagger starts.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You want a blur-to-sharp entrance: use per-word-rise or per-character-rise.\n- Only a soft masked line reveal is needed: use mask-reveal-up.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"HI, FRIEND!\\nIT IS NICE TO\\nMEET YOU.\"\n- font_size (number, 24-300): Font size, default 110\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"700\"\n- color (color): Color, default \"#2447e6\"\n- align (enum): Align, default \"left\"\n- tracking (number, -0.1-0.4): Tracking, default 0.04\n- split_by (enum): Split by, default \"characters\"\n- stagger (number, 0-0.6): Stagger, default 0.025\n- stagger_from (enum): Stagger from, default \"first\"\n- reverse (boolean): Reverse, default false\n- line_delay (number, 0-2): Line delay, default 0.5\n- start (number, 0-3): Start, default 0.2\n- stiffness (number, 50-600): Stiffness, default 200\n- damping (number, 5-60): Damping, default 21\n\nSource: https://github.com/danielpetho/fancy. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
